-- title:
--   Residue ring of O^{nr}: characteristic r and r-th powers
-- statement:
--   Let $r$ be a prime number, and let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ an irreducible element, $\mathcal O$ assumed $(\pi)$-adically complete, with residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ of cardinality $r$ and with $(r) = (\pi)$ as ideals of $\mathcal O$. Let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a commutative domain of characteristic zero which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, assumed to be adically complete for the ideal generated by the image $\pi$ of $\pi$ under $\mathcal O \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, such that this ideal is maximal, such that every $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies $p(x) \in (\pi)$ for some monic $p \in \mathcal O[X]$, and such that every monic $p \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}[X]$ of positive degree has an $x \in O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ with $p(x) \in (\pi)$. The conclusion is twofold: the quotient ring $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ has characteristic $r$, and every $a$ in this quotient is an $r$-th power, i.e. there is $b$ with $b^r = a$.
--
--   The two clauses say that the residue ring of the completed maximal unramified extension $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ of $\mathcal O$ is of characteristic $r$ and that the Frobenius on it is surjective, which is the input needed to regard it as a perfect field of characteristic $r$ and hence to invoke Witt vector / Cohen ring universal properties. It is used in the construction of the unique algebra homomorphism lifting a surjection with nilpotent-type kernel data, in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_FormalOmega_charP_residue_and_forall_exists_pow_eq.lean

